t":[{"type":"text","text":"TreeRestoreSpan carries a tree node run from a single deletion, addressed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by TreeNodeID identity, for identity-preserving Tree undo\/redo. Unlike the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text RestoreSpan (flat offsets), a tree span records the node’s structure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(type\/attrs) and its position anchors, because in a tree id-order is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sibling-order: left_sibling_id and right_sibling_id are redundant external"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary anchors of the deleted run, so restore can reconstruct the run’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internal order from the op’s own spans and needs only one surviving"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary to place it. value\/attributes are a deep copy so a GC-purged node"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be recreated."}],"title":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","type":"topic"},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan/init(serializedBytes:extensions:partial:options:)-7lhws":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Bytes"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"serializedBytes"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bytes"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"extensions"},{"kind":"text","text":": (any "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ExtensionMap","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SwiftProtobuf12ExtensionMapP"},{"kind":"text","text":")?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"partial"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"options"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"ki